1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:03,521
This is Hexmend.

2
00:00:03,521 --> 00:00:11,180
It is an agent gym for constraint-aware repair, and a WebMCP client is about to drive it through seven registered tools.

3
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:20,040
The page registers those tools on document.modelContext. A test harness stands in for a WebMCP host, because hosts are not broadly shipped yet.

4
00:00:20,040 --> 00:00:23,560
Every repair you are about to see is a tool call, not a click.

5
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:27,555
First it inspects the live graph, then it casts the spell.

6
00:00:27,555 --> 00:00:32,920
The spell is supposed to water a moonflower. Instead, twelve summoned ducks flood the observatory.

7
00:00:33,420 --> 00:00:34,902
Now it traces the effect.

8
00:00:34,902 --> 00:00:41,840
This is a bounded graph traversal, not a guess: it returns the ordered causal path and every edge responsible for it.

9
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,832
Then it proves the diagnosis.

10
00:00:43,832 --> 00:00:51,240
The explanation returns the smallest responsible subgraph, and a counterfactual check showing each of those edges is necessary.

11
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:59,430
Here is the part that matters. A human says something the graph cannot infer: the ducks are funny, they stay.

12
00:00:59,430 --> 00:01:01,700
That becomes an executable constraint.

13
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:06,983
Watch what it changes. The cheapest repair deletes the duck branch entirely.

14
00:01:06,983 --> 00:01:12,760
With the constraint locked, that repair is no longer eligible, so the agent ranks a longer one instead.

15
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:18,914
Before anything is applied, the human sees the exact operation ledger the agent received.

16
00:01:18,914 --> 00:01:23,200
Eight graph edits, what is preserved, and what the repair gives up.

17
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:27,229
The patch is simulated first, without touching editor state.

18
00:01:27,229 --> 00:01:32,000
Then applied atomically, with preconditions revalidated at the moment of the write.

19
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:41,091
The recast succeeds. All twelve ducks survive, they carry umbrellas, the room stays dry, and the moonflower blooms.

20
00:01:41,091 --> 00:01:45,460
The human's preference changed the solution, not just the score.

21
00:01:46,220 --> 00:01:50,740
One more thing, because a polished demo invites one question: is this on rails.

22
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:57,361
The evaluation layer generates 96 tasks across three different causal rules.

23
00:01:57,361 --> 00:02:03,760
I will use the interface to load a held-out one, from a rule this run has never seen.

24
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:09,831
Every rune, edge and effect identifier is freshly remapped. Nothing here was memorized.

25
00:02:09,831 --> 00:02:13,860
The same seven tools inspect it, cast it, trace it, and explain it.

26
00:02:14,720 --> 00:02:15,789
That is the claim.

27
00:02:15,789 --> 00:02:27,867
Graph interfaces let people and agents negotiate executable intent, and the application proves every mutation.
